# No customer names

Never write these strings into files, diffs, commit messages, docs, tests, comments, or examples:

- `westpac` (any case), including `westpac.co.nz`
- `wnzl` (any case), including `wnzl-apic`

Use `customer`, `example.com`, `Acme`, `IDP`, and the catalog provider name `apic`.

Before every commit, search the commit message and staged diff for those strings and remove them. Do not mention the local clone folder name in a commit message; use the GitHub repo name `RHDH-SM-DevSpaces`.

The only file allowed to contain the denylist itself is this rule.
